   "reasoning_summary": "The 13C data show a beta-glucopyranoside (104.5, 78.2, 78.0, 75.1, 71.6, 62.8) and a conjugated cyclohexenone (202.6 C=O, 168.7 Cq=, 123.6 CH=, H 6.13). This leaves a C10H15O3 aglycone with 4 DoU in total (sugar ring, enone ring, C=O, C=C). Two methyl singlets (1.14/1.04; 28.9/27.2) and Cq 36.4 indicate a gem-dimethyl group. The 49.8 CH2 (2.29/2.04) is alpha to the C=O, and 48.1 is an allylic CH (2.67). Two oxygenated CH2 groups are present: 70.0, assigned to the allylic CH2-OGlc (4.46/4.18), and 65.1, assigned to CH2OH. This gives 14 aglycone C-H and 7 sugar C-H, and with 5 OH the total matches H26. The remaining sugar protons are at 3.12-3.24 and partly hidden under the solvent peak at 3.31."
